CAT = "sqeAccounts"; SEG = "ACC"
Q = [
("A firm receives a buyer client's deposit for a purchase. Where must the money go?",
 "Into client account promptly", ["Into business account first", "Into a partner's own account", "Into it at month end"],
 "Rule 2.3 SRA Accounts Rules requires client money to be paid promptly into a client account, unless an exception applies."),
("Before taking its fees from money held in client account, what must the firm do?",
 "Send a bill or written notice", ["Get the COFA's approval", "Wait for the matter to end", "Tell the SRA in advance"],
 "Rule 4.3 requires the firm to give the client a bill of costs or other written notification of the costs before transferring client money to pay them."),
("How often must a firm reconcile its client account with the bank statements?",
 "Every five weeks at least", ["At least every quarter", "At least every two weeks by law", "Once a year at audit"],
 "Rule 8.3 requires client account reconciliations at least every five weeks, signed off by the COFA or a manager."),
("On a probate matter, one payment covers billed fees and an unpaid counsel's fee. What must the firm do?",
 "Allocate each part promptly", ["Keep it all in business account", "Hold all of it as client money", "Return it to the payer"],
 "A mixed payment containing client money goes into client account, and under rule 4.2 each part must then be allocated promptly to the correct account; an unpaid professional disbursement is client money, billed fees are not."),
("A client asks the firm to hold money and pay his household bills, unrelated to any matter. May it?",
 "No, that is banking", ["Yes, if he signs consent", "Yes, if a partner agrees", "Only up to a small sum"],
 "Rule 3.3 forbids using a client account to provide banking facilities; payments in and out must relate to the delivery of regulated services."),
("Sale proceeds are held for a client for some months. What interest must the firm account for?",
 "A fair sum", ["The bank's full rate plus 2%", "None, unless asked", "Only over a set amount"],
 "Rule 7.1 requires a fair sum of interest on client money held, unless the client agrees otherwise in writing (rule 7.2)."),
("A cashier wrongly paid a firm's bill from client money. What must the firm do on finding it?",
 "Replace the money promptly", ["Wait for the annual report", "Ask the client to top it up", "Note it for next year"],
 "Rule 6.1 requires breaches to be corrected promptly on discovery, including replacing money improperly withdrawn, and material breaches must be reported."),
("For how long must a firm keep its accounting records under the SRA Accounts Rules?",
 "At least six years", ["At least two years", "At least twelve years", "Until the matter closes"],
 "Rule 13.1 requires accounting records to be kept for at least six years."),
]
